00:17:55,637 --> 00:17:59,956
several of the men were shaken out of their hammocks. Captain Davis, who lay

214
00:17:59,957 --> 00:18:05,557
with his head on a gun, was thrown out of his cabin. End quote. Lionel then

215
00:18:05,558 --> 00:18:10,199
goes on to impute the shock to an earthquake and seems to substantiate the

216
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:15,239
imputation by stating that a great earthquake somewhere about that time did

217
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:19,717
actually do great mischief along the Spanish land. But I should not much

218
00:18:19,718 --> 00:18:24,359
wonder if in the darkness of that early hour of the morning the shock was after

219
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:30,118
all caused by an unseen whale vertically bumping the hull from beneath.

220
00:18:30,119 --> 00:18:34,359
I might proceed with several more examples, one way or another, known to

221
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:39,476
me of the great power and malice at times of the sperm whale. In more than

222
00:18:39,477 --> 00:18:43,956
one instance, he has been known not only to chase the asailing boats back to

223
00:18:43,957 --> 00:18:48,598
their ships, but to pursue the ship itself, and long withstand all the

224
00:18:48,599 --> 00:18:53,956
lances hurled at him from its decks. The English ship Pusy Hall can tell a story

225
00:18:53,957 --> 00:18:59,158
on that head. And as for his strength, let me say that there have been examples

226
00:18:59,159 --> 00:19:03,636
where the lines attached to a running sperm whale have in a calm been

227
00:19:03,637 --> 00:19:07,956
transferred to the ship and secured there, the whale towing her great hull

228
00:19:07,957 --> 00:19:12,918
through the water as a horse walks off with a cart. Again, it is very often

229
00:19:12,919 --> 00:19:18,438
observed that if the sperm whale, once struck, is allowed time to rally, then

230
00:19:18,439 --> 00:19:23,476
he acts not so often with blind rage as with willful, deliberate designs of

231
00:19:23,477 --> 00:19:28,039
destruction to his pursuers, nor is it without conveying some eloquent

232
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:32,359
indication of his character, that upon being attacked he will frequently open

233
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:36,918
his mouth and retain it in that dread expansion for several consecutive

234
00:19:36,919 --> 00:19:42,519
minutes. But I must be content with only one more and a concluding illustration,

235
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:47,079
a remarkable and most significant one, by which you will not fail to see that

236
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:52,278
not only is the most marvelous event in this book corroborated by plain facts of

237
00:19:52,279 --> 00:19:57,476
the present day, but that these marvels, like all marvels, are mere repetitions

238
00:19:57,477 --> 00:20:03,717
of the ages, so that for the millionth time we say amen with Solomon, verily

239
00:20:03,718 --> 00:20:07,476
there is nothing new under the sun.

240
00:20:07,477 --> 00:20:12,438
In the sixth Christian century lived Precopius, a Christian magistrate of

241
00:20:12,439 --> 00:20:17,079
Constantinople in the days when Justinian was emperor and Belliserius

242
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:22,839
general. As many know, he wrote the history of his own times, a work every

243
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:27,717
way of uncommon value. By the best authorities, he has always been

244
00:20:27,718 --> 00:20:32,758
considered a most trustworthy and unexaggerating historian, except in some

245
00:20:32,759 --> 00:20:36,679
one or two particulars, not at all affecting the matter presently to be

246
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:42,278
mentioned. Now in this history of his, Precopius mentions that during the term

247
00:20:42,279 --> 00:20:47,158
of his prefixure at Constantinople, a great sea monster was captured in the

248
00:20:47,159 --> 00:20:51,956
neighboring propontis or sea of Marmura after having destroyed vessels at

249
00:20:51,957 --> 00:20:57,158
intervals in those waters for a period of more than 50 years. A fact thus set

250
00:20:57,159 --> 00:21:02,039
down in substantial history cannot easily be gained, nor is there any

251
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:06,839
reason that it should be. of what precise species this sea monster was is

252
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:11,717
not mentioned, but as he destroyed ships as well as for other reasons, he must

253
00:21:11,718 --> 00:21:16,918
have been a whale, and I am strongly inclined to think a sperm whale, and I

254
00:21:16,919 --> 00:21:22,118
will tell you why. For a long time, I fancied that the sperm whale had been

255
00:21:22,119 --> 00:21:27,079
always unknown in the Mediterranean and the deep waters connecting with it. Even

256
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:32,118
now I am certain that those seas are not and perhaps never can be in the present

257
00:21:32,119 --> 00:21:37,717
constitution of things a place for his habitual gregarious resort. But further

258
00:21:37,718 --> 00:21:42,199
investigations have recently proved to me that in modern times there have been

259
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:47,397
isolated instances of the presence of the sperm whale in the Mediterranean. I

260
00:21:47,398 --> 00:21:52,278
am told on good authority that on the Barbar Coast a Commodore Davis of the

261
00:21:52,279 --> 00:21:57,717
British Navy found the skeleton of a sperm whale. Now, as a vessel of war

262
00:21:57,718 --> 00:22:03,239
readily passes through the dinels, hence a sperm whale could by the same route

263
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:07,239
pass out of the Mediterranean into the proponts.

264
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:12,039
In the propont, as far as I can learn, none of that peculiar substance called

265
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:17,239
Brit is to be found, the element of the right whale. But I have every reason to

266
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:22,438
believe that the food of the sperm whale, squid, or cuttlefish, lurks at

267
00:22:22,439 --> 00:22:26,918
the bottom of that sea, because large creatures, but by no means the largest

268
00:22:26,919 --> 00:22:32,118
of that sort, have been found at its surface. If then you properly put these

269
00:22:32,119 --> 00:22:36,839
statements together and reason upon them a bit, you will clearly perceive that

270
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:41,877
according to all human reasoning, Precopius's sea monster that for half a

271
00:22:41,878 --> 00:22:52,080
century stove the ships of a Roman emperor must in all probability have been a sperm whale.
